  "description": "Conversion of integral garage to habitable accommodation & increase flat roof height (Application for a Certificate of Lawful Development for an Proposed Use)",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed partial garage conversion to habitable accommodation does not constitute permitted development by virtue of the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) as Condition 6 of Planning Permission ref: 12176/C/93/1831 (Erection of a single storey front, side and rear extension), dated 25-02-94, restricts the use of the garage to the accommodation of private motor vehicles.",
    "The proposed raising of the existing flat roof on the side elevation facing 34 Kewferry Road does not constitute permitted development by virtue of the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 as the flat roof forms part of the single storey front, side and rear extension approved under Planning Permission ref: 12176/C/93/1831, dated 25-02-94, and therefore Planning Permission is required for alterations to the single storey front, side and rear extension approved under Planning Permission ref: 12176/C/93/1831, dated 25-02-94."
  ],
